# IMPLEMENTATION_STEPS: cu-002

1. In `pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/infrastructure/source/JsonSourceManifestReader.scala`, create this file. It reads one JSON array of candidate objects; missing `title` or `provenance` decode as None through circe's Option decoder.



```scala

package newspipe.infrastructure.source



import io.circe.parser.parse

import newspipe.application.ports.SourceManifestReader

import newspipe.domain.models.SourceCandidate

import newspipe.domain.models.SourceValidationModels.given



import java.nio.file.Files

import java.nio.file.Path



final class JsonSourceManifestReader extends SourceManifestReader:

  def read(path: String): Either[String, List[SourceCandidate]] =

    val file: Path = Path.of(path)

    if !Files.isRegularFile(file) then Left("manifest not found: " + path)

    else

      val raw: String = Files.readString(file)

      parse(raw).left.map(_.getMessage).flatMap { json =>

        json.as[List[SourceCandidate]].left.map(error => "manifest " + path + ": " + error.getMessage)

      }

```



Prove: `cd pipelines/ingestion && sbt compile` prints `[success] Compiled`.



Do NOT touch: pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/application/ports/Ports.scala, pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/domain/models/SourceValidationModels.scala, pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/infrastructure/source/JavaHttpFeedProbe.scala, pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/infrastructure/source/RomeFeedValidator.scala, pipelines/ingestion/src/main/scala/newspipe/infrastructure/source/JsonValidationResultStore.scala, conf/feeds.conf, pipelines/ingestion/src/test/**



